  "query_preview": "/THURSDAY NIGHT THROUGH TUESDAY/...\nIssued at 221 AM CDT Wed Sep 2 2026\n\nThe LREF continues to show the upper ridge building over the central \nCONUS with the upper flow becoming northwesterly over Missouri and \nIllinois by the weekend.  The models have been consistent keeping \n850mb temperatures around 22C through Saturday before a weak cold \nfront moves east across the area Saturday night.  The NBM 25th/75th \npercentile forecast at St. Louis for both Saturday and Sunday is now \nonly showing a 4-5 degree spread.  This supports keeping the \nadvisory going through Saturday before both temperatures and \ndewpoints fall slightly on Sunday which will push the heat index \nbelow advisory criteria.  Even with this said, there does remain \nsome uncertainty this far out as both the GFS/ECMWF are hinting at a \nMCS moving southeast over the area on Saturday.  This is supported \nby 20-35% of the LREF members producing rain at St. Louis over the \nweekend. However, any \"cooling\" effects of the rain could be \ncountered by moisture pooling by the incoming front which would \nboost dewpoints. As we go into early next week, less than 20% of the \nLREF members have any rain chances as the upper ridge begins to \nbuild back into the Midwest. Highs are forecast to stay in the 90s, \nthough forecast slightly lower dewpoints should keep heat indexes \nbelow 100 degrees.",
